# A progressive download slower than the clip, then stalled (cavekit-flash.md R8, T-578). flash-serve.py's /slow/ path
# sends the Spark 240 clip (65 kB a second of media) at 40 kB a second and stops for 10 s once 500 kB are out: the
# player must run its buffer dry (NetStream.Buffer.Empty), fill it again when the bytes come (Buffer.Full) and play on
# to the clip's end with the plugin alive throughout. At 40 kB a second the 1.3 MB take 33 s, with the stall 43 s.
id: flash-video-slow
section: Flash
item: A Flash video whose download is slower than the clip and then stalls for 10 s runs its buffer dry, recovers when the bytes come and plays to its end, the plugin alive throughout
shells: enyo mochi mojo
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-flash-instr.html?movie=avm2&vars=video=http://192.168.1.245:8097/slow/40000/500000/10/video/gen-spark-240.flv
kit: cavekit-flash.md R8
wait text vmeta "codec=2" 30
wait text video "video t=" 15
expect flash-drawn m yes
wait text vstatus "Buffer.Empty" 40
expect plugin 3 alive
wait text vstatus "Buffer.Full" 30
sample dry m
wait differs m dry 10
wait text vend "Play.Stop" 80
expect number vendtime 17.5 20.5
expect flash-drawn m yes
expect plugin 3 alive
